  "title": "Kourovka problem 18.97 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let G be a periodic Zassenhaus group, that is, a two-transitive permutation\ngroup with trivial stabilizer of every three points. Suppose that the stabilizer of a\npoint is a Frobenius group with locally finite kernel U containing an involution. Is it\ntrue that U is a 2-group? This was proved for finite groups by Feit. N. M. Suchkov",
